Yes, exactly. If the context is too large, Claude CLI will exit non-zero and we catch that:

```go
var exitErr *exec.ExitError
if errors.As(err, &exitErr) {
    return nil, fmt.Errorf("claude CLI failed (exit %d): %s", exitErr.ExitCode(), stderr.String())
}
```

The user will see an error like "claude CLI failed (exit 1): context length exceeded..." rather than getting partial/corrupted results. Graceful failure.

